Before the Midterm (means difficulties)
• Process Analysis
– Fundamentals of Process Analysis;
 Application of Process Analysis.
• Quality Management
– Control Charts;
– Six Sigma.
• Resource Management
 Decision Tree Method;
Linear Programming Formulation;
 LP Excel Solver.
• Service Management
– Fundamentals of Service Management;
-Queuing Model;
– Simulating Service System.

After Mid-Term:
• Inventory Management
– Newsvendor Problem;
– Economic Order Quantity (EOQ);
– More on Inventory Models.
• Demand and Revenue Management
– Forecasting Methods;
– Capacity-based Control;
– Price-based Control.
• Supply Chain Management
– Introduction to Supply Chain Management;
Supply Chain Coordination via Contracts;
 Supply Chain Mis-coordination and Achieving Strategic Fit.
• Business Model Innovation

************
Please be familiar with using the solver to calculate the questions regarding linear programming. ( Students who have studied RMBI 1020 will have the advantage) Sometimes, the solver will not work properly when your formula is too complex or does not follow the standard of the linear solver.
I did lose all marks in mid-term regarding these two areas...

Also, you are required to generate the sensitivity analysis and understand the concept of shallow price, and some difficult questions regarding the capacity. Reviewing the past paper can help you a lot.

